    "title": "Palestine Action barrister's prosecution criticised as 'chilling'",
    "summary": "CBA chair says contempt charge over closing speech by Rajiv Menon KC has left lawyers fearful of doing their job. The prosecution of a leading human rights barrister for contempt of court over his closing speech during a trial of Palestine Action activists has left lawyers fearful of doing their job, the chair of the Criminal Bar Association (CBA) has said. Rajiv Menon KC, who was acting for the defence, is due to stand trial next week, accused of breaching the judge's directions in the trial of six people for a direct action protest at an arms factory of the Israeli subsidiary Elbit Systems UK in Filton, near Bristol, in 2024.",
